# Copy this file to `.env` in the repo root and fill in the values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit it, never paste its contents into a chat,
# a ticket, or a screenshot. The service-role key below bypasses row-level
# security on the database: anyone holding it can read and write every table.
#
# Where the values come from: the Render dashboard for this service, under
# Environment. That is the authoritative copy, because it is what production
# actually runs on. Supabase's own dashboard (Project settings > API) has the
# URL and keys too if Render is missing one.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED to run the design surfaces. `/design/matchup-live`,
# `/design/market` and `/design/board-row` are client-side fixtures and work on
# a bare clone. You need this file for connected-league work: signing in,
# agreement editing, and anything that reads the real database.


# ── Required for connected-league work ────────────────────────────────────

# The only true secret in this file. No default exists in the source, on
# purpose. Without it `getSupabaseAdmin()` returns null and every admin-side
# read is skipped.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Optional: these already have committed defaults ───────────────────────
# server/services/supabaseAdmin.js falls back to the project URL and the
# publishable anon key, so you only need these to point at a different
# Supabase project.

# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Optional: local conveniences ──────────────────────────────────────────

# Guards the projections admin. Defaults to a dev password when unset, which
# is fine locally and must be set in production.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Port for the API server. Defaults to 8799.
# PORT=

# ── Optional: features that stay off unless configured ────────────────────

# ESPN league connect via the login worker.
# ESPN_LOGIN_ENABLED=
# ESPN_LOGIN_WORKER_URL=
# ESPN_CRED_KEY=

# Narrated trade rationale. The endpoint returns its grounded, structured
# rationale with or without these; they only enable the prose layer.
# TRADE_RATIONALE_API_KEY=
# TRADE_RATIONALE_MODEL=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
